  "post": {
    "caption": "Analog Devices stock fell 17.37% to $312.95 on Tuesday after record quarterly sales of $4.37B (+42%) came with a flat forecast of about $4.4B for next quarter.\nThe Motley Fool says its factories already run at full capacity, and new capacity won't make chips until the second half of 2028. Margins also dip on pricier parts and holiday shutdowns.\n\nGet this week's five, free every Saturday → link in bio.\n\n#analogdevices #adi #semiconductors #chipstocks #earnings\n\nSources: The Motley Fool (Nov 24), Analog Devices Q4 FY2026 results (8-K, Nov 24), StockTitan market close (Nov 24). Market value loss is an estimate (price drop × shares outstanding). Not investment advice."
  },
